ta","data":[{"unit":1,"title":3,"area":113,"prev":115,"next":28,"titles":117,"firmware":287},{"id":2,"title":3,"aliases":4,"area":12,"order":13,"path":14,"context":15,"summary":21,"status":22,"firmware":23,"facts":29,"procedures":58,"parameters":78,"related":79,"body":83,"sources":84,"official_url":33,"controls":92},"sequencer.bars-and-length","Bars and pattern length",[5,6,7,8,9,10,11],"add a bar","duplicate a bar","switch bars","pages","sequence length","pattern length","number of steps","sequencer",64,"knowledge/manual/units/sequencer/bars-and-length.md",{"modes":16,"screens":19},[17,18],"instrument","auxiliary",[20],"bar","`bar + [+]` adds a 16-step bar (four at most), `bar + [-]` removes one, `bar + shift + [+]` duplicates, tapping `bar` switches bars, and `bar + step n` sets how many steps the last bar plays.","current",{"min":24,"changed_in":25,"guide_version":27,"verified_on":28},"1.0.9",[26],"1.1.3","1.1.15",null,[30,35,38,43,47,50,53],{"id":31,"text":32,"source":33,"firmware_min":28,"verified_on":28,"confidence":34},"add-remove","`bar + [+]` adds a bar of 16 steps and `bar + [-]` removes one; a pattern holds at most four bars.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/sequencer#extend-with-bar","official",{"id":36,"text":37,"source":33,"firmware_min":28,"verified_on":28,"confidence":34},"duplicate","`bar + shift + [+]` duplicates the current bar; in a two-bar pattern it doubles the phrase, copying bar 1 to bar 3 and bar 2 to bar 4.",{"id":39,"text":40,"source":41,"firmware_min":28,"verified_on":28,"confidence":42},"duplicate-1-0","In a tutorial on OS 1.0.38 or older, `bar + shift + [+]` added one copy of the last bar per press instead, up to four bars; three presses turned one bar into four identical bars.","docs/research/73-overnight-run.md#log","community",{"id":44,"text":45,"source":46,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":28,"confidence":34},"duplicate-content","Since OS 1.1.3, duplicated bars keep their step components and parameter locks.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.1.3",{"id":48,"text":49,"source":33,"firmware_min":28,"verified_on":28,"confidence":34},"switch","Tapping `bar` changes which bar the step keys show; a bar picked during playback or recording stays on the keys instead of following the playhead.",{"id":51,"text":52,"source":33,"firmware_min":28,"verified_on":28,"confidence":34},"length","Holding `bar` and pressing a step key sets how many steps the pattern plays; with several bars it trims the final bar only.",{"id":54,"text":55,"source":56,"firmware_min":28,"verified_on":28,"confidence":57},"range","Bars and length together allow any pattern length from 1 to 64 steps.","docs/research/10-xy-format.md#44-constraints-and-limits","community-verified",[59,66,72],{"id":60,"goal":61,"preconditions":62,"steps":63,"result":28,"source":33,"firmware_min":28,"verified_on":28,"confidence":34},"add","Add or remove a bar",[],[64],{"keys":65,"note":28,"set":28},"bar + [+]/[-]",{"id":36,"goal":67,"preconditions":68,"steps":69,"result":28,"source":33,"firmware_min":28,"verified_on":28,"confidence":34},"Duplicate the current bar",[],[70],{"keys":71,"note":28,"set":28},"bar + shift + [+]",{"id":51,"goal":73,"preconditions":74,"steps":75,"result":28,"source":33,"firmware_min":28,"verified_on":28,"confidence":34},"Set the pattern's length in steps",[],[76],{"keys":77,"note":28,"set":28},"bar + step n",[],[80,81,82],"sequencer.bar-menu","sequencer.track-scale","basics.patterns-scenes-songs","Duplicate the first bar, then change a detail in the copy. Length makes odd patterns easy: 12 steps\nfor a bar of 3/4. The OS changelog calls bars \"pages\".",[85,87,89,91],{"url":33,"kind":86},"guide",{"url":41,"kind":88},"research",{"url":46,"kind":90},"changelog",{"url":56,"kind":88},[93,94,95,96,97,98,99,100,101,102,103,104,105,106,107,108,109,110,111,112],"key.bar","key.plus","key.minus","key.shift","step.1","step.2","step.3","step.4","step.5","step.6","step.7","step.8","step.9","step.10","step.11","step.12","step.